<title>CANADA: CanOxy appoints high-profile directors.</title>
<headline>CanOxy appoints high-profile directors.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Occidental Petroleum Ltd on Tuesday appointed two high-profile Canadian executives to oversee its business, naming Kevin Jenkins and John Willson as directors.</p>
<p>Jenkins is president and chief executive of Alberta research and development firm Westaim Corp and was the often-controversial top officer at Canadian Airlines Corp during the carrier's turbulent days of restructuring in the first half of the 1990s.</p>
<p>Willson is president and chief executive of Vancouver-based Placer Dome Inc, one of Canada's largest international mining companies. ((Reuters Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
